**Educational Institution Overview: Academic Excellence Initiative**

The Academic Excellence Initiative (AEI) is dedicated to enhancing the quality of education across various educational institutions, including K-12 schools and universities in the Greater Chicago Area. With a focus on curriculum development, student services, and accreditation processes, AEI collaborates with organizations like the Illinois State Board of Education (ISBE) and the Higher Learning Commission (HLC) to ensure compliance with educational standards.

**Curriculum Development**

AEI’s curriculum development team, led by Dr. Sarah Thompson, partners with local school districts such as Chicago Public Schools (CPS) and Evanston/Skokie School District 65 to implement evidence-based practices. The curriculum is aligned with the Common Core State Standards (CCSS) and aims to integrate technology and critical thinking skills.

